  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: arbitrary Ex command execution during C omni-completion:\n     escaping only \"/\" and \"\\\\\" in the typeref/typename tag field was not\n     enough. With no \"/\" in the payload an unclosed \"[\" makes :vimgrep's\n     pattern skipping fail, after which the command parser treats a following\n     \"|\" as a command separator, so a crafted tags entry still runs arbitrary\n     Ex/OS commands when C omni-completion is invoked on a hostile .c file.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-73073.patch: match the type field literally\n       with \\V ... \\m around escape(typename, '/\\') when building the\n       :vimgrep pattern in s:StructMembers(), in\n       runtime/autoload/ccomplete.vim; matches upstream patch 9.2.0845.\n     - CVE-2026-73073",
